+# Validate PlaceBlock arguments with t
+
+Adds the [t](https://github.com/osyrisrblx/t) runtime type checker and uses it in the PlaceBlock
+handler in place of hand-written argument checks. Remotes added later can build their validators
+the same way.
+
+## Before testing
+
+`pesde.lock` and `roblox_packages/` are **not** updated in this branch. Until you install, the
+server script fails on `require(ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t)`.
+
+1. Stop `rojo serve` if it is running.
+2. Run `pesde install` from the repo root.
+3. Commit the updated `pesde.lock` to this branch.
+4. Restart `rojo serve` and reconnect the Rojo plugin.
+5. Check that `ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t` exists in Studio before you playtest.
+
+## Changes
+
+- **`pesde.toml`**: adds `t = { wally = "osyrisrblx/t", version = "=3.1.1" }`, installed from Wally
+  through pesde the same way as the other packages. 3.1.1 is the latest version on the Wally index,
+  pinned exactly like the other packages.
+- **`README.md`**: adds t to the packages table.
+- **`src/ServerScriptService/BlockPlacement.server.luau`**: the argument checks are now one
+  validator:
+
+  ```lua
+  local isPlaceBlockArgs = t.tuple(t.keyOf(BlockTypes.ByName), t.intersection(t.Vector3, isNotNaN))
+  ```
+
+## Checks kept
+
+| Before | After |
+|---|---|
+| `typeof(blockTypeName) ~= "string"` | `t.keyOf(BlockTypes.ByName)`: `ByName` has only string keys, so a non-string never matches |
+| `BlockTypes.ByName[blockTypeName]` is nil | `t.keyOf(BlockTypes.ByName)`: the name must be one of its keys |
+| `typeof(position) ~= "Vector3"` | `t.Vector3` |
+| `position ~= position` (NaN in any component) | `isNotNaN`, the same self-inequality check, combined with `t.intersection` |
+
+The rest of the handler stays the same: the rate limit, the character and `HumanoidRootPart`
+check, `cell.Y < 0`, the occupied cell check, and `MAX_REACH`. The snapped cell is now computed
+right after validation instead of after the character check. It is a pure calculation, so behavior
+does not change. Luau can't narrow types through a t validator, so the handler casts the two
+validated arguments (`:: string`, `:: Vector3`).
+
+## Testing
+
+None of this has been run yet: no install, analysis, lint, or playtest. After the steps above:
+
+- Run the checks in the README (`rojo sourcemap ...`, `luau-lsp analyze ...`, `selene src`,
+  `stylua --check src`).
+- Playtest and place blocks of each type, which should still work.
+- From the client command bar, fire bad arguments. None of these should place a block or raise a
+  server error:
+  - `game.ReplicatedStorage.PlaceBlock:FireServer(123, Vector3.zero)`
+  - `game.ReplicatedStorage.PlaceBlock:FireServer("Lava", Vector3.new(0, 4, 0))`
+  - `game.ReplicatedStorage.PlaceBlock:FireServer("Brick", "not a vector")`
+  - `game.ReplicatedStorage.PlaceBlock:FireServer("Brick", Vector3.new(0/0, 4, 0))`
+  - `game.ReplicatedStorage.PlaceBlock:FireServer("Brick")`
+
